{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-14T09:26:13.427Z","author":"codex-toolchain-1114b","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"118a9002071e231c67817b09","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-14T09:26:13.427Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-14T09:26:13.424Z","author":"codex-toolchain-1114b","text":"Baseline current pm-cli 2026.11.14 and pm-changelog 2026.11.13 reproduces corpus.test.ts: 7 pass, 7 fail, including all four named scenarios plus containment rechecks, bounded fits and no-git training. GH-1665 normalizes declared spellings to camel-case SDK keys; underscore options are undeclared, so required-option validation precedes the handler. Keep every filesystem refusal and race witness using supported SDK keys; add explicit host refusal/no-write checks. The historical failed CI log also shows required-option message assertions in domain, benchmark, lineage and loop tests; reproduce and adapt those without weakening matchers. Only this tracker item is owned; recursive-training items remain untouched."}]}],"before_hash":"1ec4111b2ddb38e8b0efafd9855a697c544a2212e16ee0df6832c630512a09cc","after_hash":"59bd2b79492deaf1b534fb6aa316bb44303afd5e025ffd86ddecbf721f085ee4","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"2a4b046981492db96ee668390ca84b4c9c7d8ef6e7286a3c3907565cd1602491"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-14T09:35:51.275Z","author":"codex-toolchain-1114b","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"118a9002071e231c67817b09","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-14T09:35:51.273Z","author":"codex-toolchain-1114b","text":"Installed public SDK declarations in sdk/extension/command-options.d.ts document canonical camel-case keys, direct spelling normalization and required/unknown validation. Two synthetic pm-cli 2026.11.14 probes are upstream candidates, not filed: (1) a missing required flag yields PmCliError with exitCode 2 but code undefined and context {}, so exact message plus absent-code plus no-write witnesses replace handler-message assertions; (2) a declared required fromTracker plus undeclared typo or from_tracker is dispatched with both keys, despite unknown-option refusal being documented. Canonical handler reads ignore those undeclared values and remain correct if a future host refuses them first. Searches for extension required option code and unknown_option harness returned no issues. The npm artifact omits CHANGELOG.md; reviewed the exact v2026.11.14 source changelog through 2026.11.8, including all new Migrate notes. No setup-phase linked tests are added, preserving tracker-reader compatibility."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-14T09:35:51.275Z"}],"before_hash":"59bd2b79492deaf1b534fb6aa316bb44303afd5e025ffd86ddecbf721f085ee4","after_hash":"741c2ee66e46b5e93e289075864a80a87189c83fd68cbddcd128465a9da5bafa","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_fil